msgstr ""

#: lib/policy.py:3297
msgid ""
"Return a uniform 401 HTTP status code for failed authentications, so the "
"status code cannot be used to distinguish the reason a request failed. "
"Combine with \"hide_specific_error_message\" (in the authentication "
"scope) to also mask the error message. WARNING: This changes the HTTP "
"status codes returned by the /auth and /validate endpoints (e.g. "
"400/403/404 all become 401). Clients, proxies or monitoring that rely on "
"the specific status codes may break. Only enable this if you understand "
"the impact on your integrations. This policy is evaluated without "
"user/realm/resolver/time conditions (client IP and user agent matching "
"still apply)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/policy.py:3311
msgid ""
